{
 "id": "305-49",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "At the beginning of each sprint, we hold a company-wide brainstorming session where everyone can pitch ideas and form initial teams.",
  "Keep a notebook or a digital document where you jot down these observations and potential solutions.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any further questions or if there's anything at all that I can do to support you.",
  "Transparency and open communication are key to a healthy work environment.",
  "That way, we can address them during the meeting, ensuring that all voices are heard.",
  "From now on, I want you to start attribute names with the prefix 'i_'.",
  "This is to maintain consistency with the coding standards we've established within the team.",
  "It's a small change, but it will help ensure that your code aligns with the rest of the team's and makes collaboration and code reviews easier.",
  "Don't worry about making changes to your previous commits; we can discuss the best approach for that later.",
  "For now, just focus on applying this convention moving forward.",
  "You're doing a fantastic job, and I'm always here to help however I can.",
  "Always happy to help.",
  "And feel free to reach out if you have any questions or concerns about this or anything else.",
  "When naming attributes, I'd like you to always start the attribute names with 's_' as a prefix.",
  "Additionally, include a single digit in the attribute name.",
  "This will help us maintain a consistent and distinctive naming convention.",
  "No, you can use the single digit arbitrarily.",
  "The main goal is to have concise and unique attribute names that follow this new convention."
 ],
